{
  "assessment": "The source provides a quantitative, exactly solvable transition for the Toric code under bit-flip (Pauli-X) incoherent errors, with a critical error rate p_c^(2)=0.178 and a mapping to the 2D classical Ising universality class. The open string operator W_{m\\bar{m}} is defined and its behavior in the topological and condensed phases is described. The TEE is computed as 2 log 2 below and log 2 above the transition. This supports a quantitative cluster with one control (error rate p), one readout (open string expectation value), and a mechanism with the critical parameter. The source also provides the relation mu = tanh^{-1}[p/(1-p)] and the critical mu_c = (1/4) log(1+sqrt(2)). The extraction is limited to this single best cluster; other examples (double semion, Laughlin) are qualitative and not selected. The case is authoring-ready because there is a numeric control, a numeric readout, a quantitative mechanism, and an objective source-grounded response within an explicit domain.",
